  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string SSS of length NNN, containing lowercase Latin letters. You are also given an integer KKK.\n\nYou would like to create a new string S′S'S′ by following the following process:\n\n\nFirst, partition SSS into exactly KKK non-empty subsequences S1,S2,…,SKS_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_KS1​,S2​,…,SK​. Note that every character of SSS must be present in exactly one of the SiS_iSi​.\nThen, create S′S'S′ as the concatenation of these subsequences, i.e, S′=S1+S2+…+SKS' = S_1 + S_2 + \\ldots + S_KS′=S1​+S2​+…+SK​, where +++ denotes string concatenation.\nDetermine the **lexicographically** smallest S′S'S′ that can be created.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers, NNN and KKK.\nThe second line of each test case contains the string SSS.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the lexicographically smallest string S′S'S′ that can be created.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\leq K \\leq N1≤K≤N",
      "SSS contains only lowercase Latin letters.",
      "Sum of NNN over all cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n6 1\nwhizzy\n14 2\naaacdecdebacde\n4 3\ndbca",
        "output": "whizzy\naaaaccdecdebde\nabcd",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: K=1K = 1K=1, so our only option is to set S′=S1=whizzyS' = S_1 = whizzyS′=S1​=whizzy.\nTest Case 222: Partition S=aaacdecdebacdeS = \\textcolor{red}{aaa}\\textcolor{blue}{cdecdeb}\\textcolor{red}{ac}\\textcolor{blue}{de}S=aaacdecdebacde into S1=aaaacS_1 = \\textcolor{red}{aaaac}S1​=aaaac and S2=cdecdebdeS_2 = \\textcolor{blue}{cdecdebde}S2​=cdecdebde, to form S′=aaaaccdecdebdeS' = aaaaccdecdebdeS′=aaaaccdecdebde.\nTest Case 333: Partition S=dbcaS = d\\textcolor{blue}{bc}\\textcolor{red}{a}S=dbca into S1=aS_1 = \\textcolor{red}{a}S1​=a, S2=bcS_2 = \\textcolor{blue}{bc}S2​=bc, and S3=dS_3 = dS3​=d to form S′=abcdS' = abcdS′=abcd.\nIn both test cases 222 and 333, it can be shown that no other partition gives a lexicographically smaller S′S'S′."
      }
    ]
  },
